      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 2. Temporal Patterns — How do crime frequencies vary across time dimensions (day of week, month, season), and are there identifiable cyclical patterns that persist year-over-year?"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RS3gcc81tJuh"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Findings: <br>\n",
        "Most of the crimes happen during the weekend especially on Sunday, and the time of day is spreaded within the evening. <br> A trend can be seen that at noon there is a trend of crimes happening. <br> But overall, on Fridays there are total more crimes being committed out of all the days of the week."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xitz6DwZu07C"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
        "\n",
        "df['Hour'] = df['Date'].dt.hour\n",
        "df['DayOfWeek'] = df['Date'].dt.day_name()\n",
        "\n",
        "day_order = ['Monday','Tuesday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday','Saturday','Sunday']\n",
        "pivot = df.groupby(['DayOfWeek', 'Hour']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        "pivot = pivot.reindex(day_order)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = go.Figure(data=go.Heatmap(\n",
        "    z=pivot.values,\n",
        "    x=list(pivot.columns),\n",
        "    y=pivot.index.tolist(),\n",
        "    colorscale='YlOrRd',\n",
        "    colorbar=dict(title='Crime Count')\n",
        "))\n",
        "fig.update_layout(\n",
        "    title='Crime Frequency by Day of Week and Hour',\n",
        "    xaxis_title='Hour of Day',\n",
        "    yaxis_title='Day of Week'\n",
        ")\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
